1784346391.309 RX Intersection of Temple St. & Stone St.
1784346391.311 RX     The magnificent Temple of Silvermere stands tall and proud to your west. It
1784346391.311 RX white silver-streaked marble walls are a testament to its magnificent
1784346391.311 RX construction, as does the fact that it has remained seemingly undamaged for the
1784346391.311 RX past hundred years. This is where weary folk go to have their wounds healed,
1784346391.311 RX and where holy folk receive their divine training. The Temple's large wrought
1784346391.311 RX doors are open to the public at all hours. Stone street crosses to the north
1784346391.311 RX and south here. 
1784346391.311 RX Obvious exits: north, south, east, west
1784346391.311 RX [HP=27/MA=66]:w
1784346391.312 RX look
1784346392.798 RX Temple Foyer
1784346392.799 RX     The hall's lofty roof is supported by graceful soaring archways, and the
1784346392.799 RX walls are crafted of white marble run through with silver streaks. Bright lamps
1784346392.799 RX line the walls, illuminating every dark corner here. Racks and shelves line the
1784346392.799 RX walls, for people to leave dirty cloaks or clothing. To the east are the
1784346392.799 RX Temple's ornate doors, propped open even in these uncertain times, and to the
1784346392.799 RX west, a wide passageway leads towards the inner parts of the Temple. 
1784346392.799 RX Obvious exits: east, west
1784346392.799 RX [HP=27/MA=66]:look
