1784347054.479 RX The Silver River, Silvermere Docks
1784347054.483 RX     The rapid currents of the river make it perilous to travel, even in a
1784347054.483 RX suitable vessel, as it is filled with strange water-dwellers. The shimmering
1784347054.483 RX silvery surface of the water gives the river its namesake. To the north, you
1784347054.483 RX can see the gravelly beach of a large island poking out of the middle of the
1784347054.483 RX river, and to the south, the seldom-used port of Silvermere. The river flows
1784347054.483 RX quickly downstream to the west, and upstream to the east. 
1784347054.483 RX Also here: water elemental.
1784347054.483 RX Obvious exits: north, south, east, west
1784347054.827 TX n
1784347054.832 RX [HP=56/MA=60]:n
1784347055.504 RX Island, Beach Landing
1784347055.504 RX     This is a gravelly beach bordering a small, sheltered lagoon. Off across
1784347055.504 RX the raging river, you can see the port-side of the city of Silvermere. The
1784347055.504 RX beach continues off to the east and west, curving around the sheer rock face
1784347055.504 RX which towers above you. 
1784347055.507 RX Obvious exits: south, east, west
1784347055.827 TX e
1784347055.832 RX [HP=56/MA=60]:e
1784347056.827 TX ne
1784347057.557 RX Gravelly Beach
1784347057.561 RX     This is a gravelly beach, curving around the sheer rock face to the north.
1784347057.561 RX Bits of shell and bone litter the beach, and if there is any plant life, you
1784347057.561 RX certainly cannot find it. In fact, there is a noticeable lack of life signs
1784347057.561 RX throughout this whole area, and you get the feeling that even the animals that
1784347057.561 RX may have inhabited this island have abandoned it. The beach continues to the
1784347057.561 RX northeast, and a small lagoon is to the west. 
1784347057.561 RX Obvious exits: west, northeast
