1784349896.368 RX The Silver River, Silvermere Docks
1784349896.371 RX     The rapid currents of the river make it perilous to travel, even in a
1784349896.371 RX suitable vessel, as it is filled with strange water-dwellers. The shimmering
1784349896.371 RX silvery surface of the water gives the river its namesake. To the north, you
1784349896.371 RX can see the gravelly beach of a large island poking out of the middle of the
1784349896.371 RX river, and to the south, the seldom-used port of Silvermere. The river flows
1784349896.371 RX quickly downstream to the west, and upstream to the east. 
1784349896.371 RX Obvious exits: north, south, east, west
1784349896.371 RX [HP=56/MA=66]:n
1784349896.416 RX n
1784349897.384 RX The river bashes you up against some rocks!
1784349897.391 RX Island, Beach Landing
1784349897.391 RX     This is a gravelly beach bordering a small, sheltered lagoon. Off across
1784349897.391 RX the raging river, you can see the port-side of the city of Silvermere. The
1784349897.391 RX beach continues off to the east and west, curving around the sheer rock face
